      "writtenOn": "2022-03-25T01:09:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e There should be a way to catch the exit in Python and run any arbitrary code (such as setting GPIO to a specific state). Is that what you mean or something else?\n\nSomething else.\nIn the gpiod API, once the gpio handler is done, the gpio is released to an undetermined state.\nProbably using the system commands `gpioget` and `gpioset` will be more controllable",
      "parentUuid": "bcc1c744_5ef646f2",
