      "writtenOn": "2022-03-31T23:19:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like `gpioset` and `gpioget` are provided as part of `libgpiod`. As Patryk mentioned in the first comment, there is a native Python API for `libgpio` (`import gpiod`), and [this example](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/libs/libgpiod/libgpiod.git/tree/bindings/python/examples/gpioset.py) demonstrates how you can use the API to perform the same functionality as `gpioset`. To use the Python library, you will need to make sure that there is a dependency in the [ebuild that installs `fptool.py`](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay/+/HEAD/chromeos-base/ec-utils-test/ec-utils-test-9999.ebuild#51) on [`libgpiod`](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/portage-stable/+/HEAD/dev-libs/libgpiod/libgpiod-1.4.1.ebuild), which looks like it is installing the [python bindings](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/portage-stable/+/HEAD/dev-libs/libgpiod/libgpiod-1.4.1.ebuild#28).",
      "parentUuid": "125b8245_05b837f5",
